Requirement (client JWKS endpoint): (R1) With a client-authentication key, GET in any letter case answers 200 with the key set, Cache-Control: no-store and Content-Type: application/json. (R2) Every other method answers 405 with Allow: GET and no body. (R3) Without a key (client-secret mode, the withheld form) every method answers 404 with no header and no body, indistinguishable from an unrouted path.

Repository API-Sheriff (Java 25, Quarkus). Project rules: CuiLogger only; INFO/WARN/ERROR through LogRecord constants, DEBUG may use plain strings with %s; constructor and method arguments checked with Objects.requireNonNull; no generic Exception/RuntimeException caught or thrown; records preferred for values. The class already declares the constants used (OK, NOT_FOUND, METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED, GET, CACHE_CONTROL, NO_STORE, CONTENT_TYPE, APPLICATION_JSON, ALLOW), the nullable field document (null in the withheld form) and the record JwksOutcome(int status, Map<String, String> headers, @Nullable Map<String, Object> document).

